    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0573" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/2192</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Assistant Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-01-28">January 28, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Sir Ronald Campbell<anchor n="12" xml:id="d611-f1"/> came in to see me at my
                    request.</p>
                <p>Representative Sol Bloom telephoned me just prior to Sir Ronald’s arrival that H.
                    Res. 418 and 419, regarding the opening of Palestine to immigration and its
                    constitution as a democratic Jewish commonwealth, had been introduced with both
                    Republican and Democratic support; and that he expected to put it through his
                    Committee. He asked that we speak to the British about it. I therefore said to
                    Sir Ronald that this was the situation: that, in my judgment, the support of
                    these Resolutions assured their passage; and that we thought his Government
                    should be informed. We should be glad to have any ideas they might have. I added
                    however that, in my judgment, there was real likelihood that the Resolutions
                    would be passed by a large majority, if not unanimously.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dolf</hi>] A. B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">erle</hi>], <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
